{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_a6_hierarchical_reconciliation", "label": "A6 \u00b7 Hierarchical reconciliation (Beer Hall, units)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Run for the Beer Hall only: Two River Taps is closed and Ellel is booking-driven with ~64 trading days, so their category/item splits would be sparser than the Beer Hall's already-under-covering item bands. A considered scope decision, revisitable if those venues' L1 forecasts prove operationally useful."}, {"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_wls_v", "label": "WLS_v reconciliation (Wickramasuriya et al. 2019 Eq. 11, diagonal W)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not called 'MinT': those authors reserve that name for the off-diagonal Sample/Shrink estimators, so the artefact declines the more impressive label it is not entitled to."}, {"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_dow_median_base_forecaster", "label": "Robust DOW-median base forecaster at L2/L3", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The L1 rung-climbing discipline was deliberately not repeated: the ~30 item series are too sparse to fit ETS/GBM without overfitting, and the coherence guarantee depends only on the summing matrix, not on base-forecaster sophistication \u2014 a better base would tighten bands, not change coherence."}, {"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_one_se_adoption_margin", "label": "One-standard-error adoption margin for intermittent estimators", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The bare inequality once adopted a node on a 0.21% validation margin that then scored 96% worse on test, so the estimator must now beat the DOW-median by more than one SE of the paired differential over disjoint 7-day sub-blocks. The margin was pre-registered before implementation but AFTER that observation, and that ordering is stated rather than concealed."}, {"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_reconciled_band_coverage", "label": "Reconciled-band coverage (L2 vs L3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One band-construction path serves both the coverage check and production (no separate parametric band). L3 series are sparse and noisy so their bands under-cover \u2014 declared an honest, expected limitation of conformal at that grain."}, {"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_stock_cover_join", "label": "A12 stock-cover join (inventory-aware reorder)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lines whose brand is not a forecast A6 node are omitted rather than guessed \u2014 NULL demand is reported as absent, not imputed."}, {"id": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_prereg_adoption_margin_ledger", "label": "ledger/prereg_adoption_margin_2026-08-01.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/hierarchy/reconciliation_forecast.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "brain_hierarchy_reconciliation_forecast_a6_hierarchical_reconciliation", "target": "br